# Story page: nm-easy
# {name} becomes the snake's name. Paragraphs are separated by a blank line.
title = Nightmare: Starving
---
That night {name} dreamed of the garden, only parched and cracked, with every apple a mile away and getting farther.

{name} grew smaller with every heartbeat until it was little more than a very determined noodle, which is what hunger does to all of us, in the end.

'Hunger,' boomed the coil, 'is where every story begins.' {name} would have argued, but it was too busy being hungry, which rather proved the point.
